	"data": "Concept: Refocus\n\nCaptured from audio journal 2026-04-08, elaborated by Calcifer\n\nThe Idea\n\nLinked data has n-dimensional scaling — as a knowledge graph grows, it becomes impossible to navigate in its entirety. Refocus is the ability to take a specific lens or dimension of that data and project it into a manageable 2D or 3D view for human navigation and ideation.\n\nIt's not just filtering. It's perspective-shifting on a graph.\n\nHow It Works (cithoreal's description)\nStart with a concept: \"I want…",
